Package: penguin-cpp
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Juan Francisco Gonzalez Pacheco <jfgonzalez@unimagdalena.edu.co>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS@, gcc, g++, make, gdb, astyle, clang-format, cups-client, fonts-dejavu-core, gnome-terminal | mate-terminal | xfce4-terminal | konsole | xterm | x-terminal-emulator
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/JuanFranG/Penguin-cpp
Description: simple C and C++ IDE for learning, a Linux port of Dev-C++
 Penguin cpp is an integrated development environment for C and C++ meant
 for teaching: a code editor with completion and folding, single files and
 projects built with gcc and make, programs run in a terminal, and a
 debugger on top of gdb with breakpoints, watches and step by step
 execution.
 .
 It is a port of Embarcadero Dev-C++ (Orwell and Bloodshed Dev-C++ before
 it) to Lazarus and Free Pascal. The interface is available in English,
 Spanish and other languages.
